{"reference":"Psalms 42","book":"Psalms","chapter":42,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"The Psalm’s Heading","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Psalm headings belong to a received tradition that associates psalms with figures and groups such as David, Asaph, and the sons of Korah, while also preserving labels for genre, performance, tune, instrument, or setting. Because the interpretation of these superscriptions is disputed, they should be read carefully rather than treated as an unqualified statement of authorship or occasion.","verse_refs":["Psalms 42:1"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_042_8f3e6546f12e9119eebfcc0d"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}